            "review_title": "Review at Cugini - Ristorante Italiano",
            "review_text": "SeasidersBali\nDenpasar27 contributions\n0\nFirst impressions count\nSep 2020\nAt Cugini the décor and ambiance immediately suggests that the meal will be a little special. It doesn't disappoint and an almost full house doesn’t lie. The white wine arrives promptly in a cooler without having to ask. The starters are presented artfully with thick slices of beef for the carpaccio with rocket garnish and a perfectly soft burrata. For mains the linguine di mare was cooked just as we requested (not al dente). The sea bass (brazino scottato) was superb with contrasting textures of crisp skin and white meat with a delicate sauce. The owner, Nico, made time to chat: such attention is always appreciated. His recommendation of grappa with panna cotta made a wonderful finish to the meal. We hear the menu will shortly be changing: we will certainly be back to try some of the new dishes or daily specials.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 25, 2020",
