            "review_title": "Review at Cugini - Ristorante Italiano",
            "review_text": "Agnese B\n6 contributions\n0\nSublime!\nJan 2020\nBeing an Italian girl, I don't usually eat in an Italian restaurant abroad. However, I did just an exception for one time... and it has been a really beautiful exception!\n\nI don't have any other word to describe my experience in Cugini Restaurant: \"sublime\" - which means \"Divine\".\nIt's better than lots of Italian restaurant in Italy... and I'm not kidding!\n\nThere is a special care in selecting all the ingredients and how to combine them in order to surprise the people.\nIt isn't the classic Italian Restaurant abroad, it's something different and surely better, where all the amazing dishes they offer, are the results of a strong passion. And Nico, the chef, is the main emblem of it.\nAsk for him when you go, and I'm sure you will agree with me!\n\nAll the staff' members are really kind and the service is professional and fast.\nThe restaurant is completely modern and new, with a beautiful terrace where you can enjoy a special dinner.\n\nIf you go to Tayho, you should have a stop there and try this little Italian oasis in Hanoi... it is really recommended!\n\nI suggest you to try the beef carpaccio, the mushrooms paté and the crab (as starters), and the black tortellini filled with crab. And... don't forget the dessert! Lemon tartina and profitterole are surely recommended!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 19, 2020",
