            "review_text": "RoryH1\nCape Town117 contributions\n1\nGood food let down by ridiculous pricing\nNov 2019\nI live in Hanoi and have now been to Cugini a number of times, both for lunch and dinner. I've deliberately waited until now to give them the benefit of a review based not on just one, but multiple, visits. First, the positive. Food is generally good, sometimes very good. Service is also generally good. It starts to fall apart when things get busy, but one has a sense that they are always trying their best. Now, the negative. For what it is, Cugini is a ridiculously expensive restaurant. Portion size exacerbates this. The starter portions are okay. A little on the small side, but they are starters after all. But the main courses represent laughable value. The portion sizes of the pasta, meat, and seafood dishes are barely larger than the appetizers--which makes the prices they charge especially extortionate. This complete lack of value is carried through to the wine list--bloated prices for small pours. As an example, I ordered a port with a cheese platter. I was charged 250 000.00 dong for a tiny measure of port that could not have been more than 20ml. Come on, guys! That's almost $11.00 for slightly more than a tablespoon. You should be embarrassed. And that kind of pricing is representative of the whole meal. Yes, wine is expensive in Asia, and yes, many of the ingredients are imported. But the disparity between the landed cost of these goods and the prices being charged by Cugini is utterly unjustifiable. I guess the restaurant would argue that they are not overcharging as long as people are prepared to pay their prices. And maybe its working for them now. But I suspect they're going to get squeezed out of an increasingly competitive and rapidly improving restaurant scene unless they reevaluate their pricing policy.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 18, 2019\nCypVN\nThe port you drank cost over a million dong for 50cl, it is called Otima 10 from Warre's. And, along with the meal, it was comp'd. \n\nWe charged anger management therapy and public venting. Considering that a shrink charges around 2.2 millions for 45 minutes in Hanoi, you had a real bargain.\nRead more\nWritten November 22, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
